Optiq bundles one codec binary itself, the jpegli JPEG encoder in vendor/jpegli/. It is built from source by
codecs/jpegli/build.sh, and the licence texts ship next to it (vendor/jpegli/LICENSE.*):

  jpegli                                        BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) the JPEG XL Project Authors
  Highway (in jpegli)                           Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause, Copyright Google LLC
  skcms (in jpegli)                             BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2018 Google Inc.

For SVG, Optiq depends on two more packages and ships resvg's .wasm (unmodified) in vendor/resvg/:

  svgo (svgo/browser)                           MIT, Copyright (c) Kir Belevich; the browser build bundles
                                                sax (BlueOak-1.0.0), css-tree and csso (MIT), css-select,
                                                css-what, domutils, domhandler, nth-check, entities (BSD-2-Clause),
                                                dom-serializer (MIT), boolbase (ISC)
  @resvg/resvg-wasm (resvg)                     MPL-2.0, Copyright (c) the resvg authors; source:
                                                https://github.com/yisibl/resvg-js and https://github.com/linebender/resvg ;
                                                licence text: https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/

